PATCH_ID: 002
TYPE: feature_architecture

INTENT:
Introduce dual-runtime Game Boy emulator supporting real ROM execution alongside GitHub-driven JARVIS cyberspace renderer.

CONTEXT:
System extends intake pipeline into runtime-facing architecture. Emulator must support:
1) actual Game Boy ROM playback
2) GitHub-based JARVIS modules
3) grid-based navigation shell (semantic cyberspace UI)

SCOPE:
- emulator runtime controller
- mode switching system
- GitHub FS integration hooks (read-only)
- cartridge loading system (JARVIS modules)
- grid shell navigation layer

CHANGES:

- Add ModeController with three states:
  - "gb_rom" → executes Game Boy emulator core
  - "jarvis_ui" → GitHub-driven modular UI runtime
  - "grid_home" → navigation shell (cyberspace graph view)

- Integrate Game Boy core runtime:
  - loads ROM binaries from /roms
  - isolated execution context (no GitHub access)
  - standard emulator loop (start/stop/update)

- Define JARVIS runtime layer:
  - reads /gameboy/** from GitHub
  - uses FS abstraction layer (fetch + cache system)
  - loads cartridges via manifest.json + entry.js
  - supports modular UI + intake viewer

- Introduce Grid OS shell:
  - graph-based navigation (nodes + edges)
  - nodes represent ROMs, cartridges, memory, intake, modules
  - edges represent navigation paths
  - no execution allowed in grid mode

- Define InputRouter:
  - mode-aware input dispatch
  - grid navigation when in grid_home
  - ROM control in gb_rom mode
  - UI interaction in jarvis_ui mode

- Establish strict isolation rules:
  - GB core cannot access GitHub FS
  - JARVIS cannot access ROM memory
  - Grid shell cannot execute logic, only route

- Define GitHub integration contract:
  - /gameboy/cartridges = modular UI systems
  - /gameboy/intake = GPT/Claude patch pipeline view layer
  - /gameboy/memory = snapshot storage (POSEIDON model)
  - /roms = Game Boy ROM binaries

- Add future-ready abstraction:
  - cartridges behave like sandboxed modules
  - each module exposes init/start/update lifecycle
  - API access restricted to CartridgeAPI (fs, ui, input, memory)

CONSTRAINTS:
- no implementation of actual emulator engine required in this patch
- no WebGL/TRON rendering implementation yet
- no backend or server dependency
- only structural and integration design
- maintain strict separation of runtimes

OUTPUT EXPECTATION:
- system capable of supporting:
  - real Game Boy ROM execution mode
  - GitHub-based JARVIS UI mode
  - grid navigation shell mode
- clean separation between execution, UI, and data layers
